{
  "dom_id": "step-t8731",
  "name": "Solving \"Strictly Less Than\" Inequalities",
  "problem": "Let's now think about how to graph the solutions to the inequality\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/6a25488634d209465bceb496d954cd45546091151404b8b1d4ea4b8959f32a58.svg) \n\nAs before, we start by replacing the inequality symbol ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/c1961799d574c1cdf4d3ec008eaa6a13f205bc90c75aa4c5f2b763f2fc7b26d4.svg) with an equals sign ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0390f8b1f8405fa7ec0dd6ce7af3bccd7e0474a8ed59e323595062ced4c42fcf.svg) and plot the resulting line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0959b88bad14750ae0ac71cfc63edbe90a03ae64db7fc0cb56cbf827289f11d5.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/72b217c75c8ec84681212a8ab48614fb777e05e7022ca338897d16763070c816.png)\n\nNotice that we have a \"*less than*\" ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/c1961799d574c1cdf4d3ec008eaa6a13f205bc90c75aa4c5f2b763f2fc7b26d4.svg) inequality. Therefore, we draw a *dashed* line. \n\nNow, since we're solving ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/d71368c766686c489e604c80865ad272fbae06736c14dce0d85e4636a9972ed3.svg) we need to shade all points whose ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-value is *smaller than* its ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-value. This is given by all of the points that lie *below* our dashed line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/7bf436735632fc8e848e3f76577748628cc846ef5186a97011a77c02d1b93347.png)\n\nAnd we're done! All of the points in the shaded region satisfy the inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/6a25488634d209465bceb496d954cd45546091151404b8b1d4ea4b8959f32a58.svg)\n\nTo check that we've shaded the correct region, we pick a point inside the shaded region and check that it satisfies the original inequality. Let's pick the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/ab6b2f25fb90ef8bea8b21d9d0253752c37bb3c77b675547a223b03f97d3bf6a.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/95cb11e9786be8ef669469761d9d120693d46a64b6ce4fdb0dd7eb225479b866.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/dcc19bac01833ff23365244490e52b2722741da56e804e9a95b5b264f23216bf.svg) into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/198239e0b69706444f4b76f1bd90625df630be1dc0f43f1e35f82ad216e04b29.svg) \n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region.",
